The '''Palace Courtyard''' was a large enclosure located in [[Theed]], the [[capital]] [[city]] of [[Naboo]]'s [[human]] [[Naboo (people)|inhabitants]]. Built over a part of Theed that was heavily bombed by [[Trade Federation]] [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|Armored Assault Tanks]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]], the Courtyard was meant to nurture and encourage principles of enlightened thought and practice.<ref name="SWCL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> A huge half-circle with a central islet, the courtyard featured a number of bridges and fountains. Its buildings consisted of several domed structures and a large arcing colonnade running along the courtyard's edge,<ref name="AOTC" /> whithin which a [[Hologram|holographic]] frieze depicted [[artist]]s and [[philosopher]]s from Naboo's history.<ref name="SWCL" /> It was connected to the [[Theed Royal Palace|Royal Palace]] by a long avenue known as the [[Palace Plaza]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Theed_spaceport.jpg|thumb|right|200px|The Palace Courtyard is visible opposite of the Palace in this image.<br />From ''Revenge of the Sith'', c. 2005. cf. below]]
[[File:Theed-MoaTM.png|thumb|right|200px|This image, despite inaccurately displaying the details of the [[Theed Spaceport]] and Palace Courtyard, is generally composed, in regards to the placement of structures, in the same manner. The same cannot be said for other details, however.<br />From [[Mystery of a Thousand Moons]], c. [[2009]]]]
In [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], the Palace Courtyard appeared to be located in front of the Palace and directly linked to it, which suggests that it took the place<ref name="AOTC" /> of the former Palace Plaza, which appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> However, when the [[original trilogy]] was released in [[Star Wars Trilogy (DVD)|DVD format]] in [[2004]], shots of the Palace Plaza were inserted in the ending sequence of [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']], creating a discrepancy between the movies.<ref name="ROJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> In the [[2005]] movie [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], the location of the Palace Courtyard was modified. The Courtyard opens its two arms towards the Palace Plaza, and is not part of the Palace proper.<ref name="ROS">{{Film|III}}</ref>

The brief Courtyard scene in ''Attack of the Clones'' was filmed at the [[Wikipedia:Plaza de España, Seville|Plaza de España]] in [[Wikipedia:Seville|Seville]], [[Wikipedia:Spain|Spain]] on [[September 13]], [[2000]]. In post-production, [[Industrial Light & Magic]] greatly expanded the plaza, which is a half-circle, to create what is seen in the movie.<ref name="Galactic Backpacking 5">{{SW|url=news/galactic-backpacking-part-5-visiting-real-world-theed-plaza|text=Galactic Backpacking, Part 5: Visiting Real-World Theed Plaza|nolive=1}}</ref>

